// 07-10 Task 1 (WR-01's user-visible half, D-07-50): `check` does not
// diagnose duplicate `fn` declarations at all -- both `helper` declarations
// below are assigned the SAME semanticID (check.go's `semanticID` is a pure
// function of module+kind+name, with no uniqueness check across
// declarations), so `check.Program` emits two `core.Function` entries that
// share one function ID. `buildCalleeContracts` is a
// `map[string]calleeContract` keyed by declared NAME and populated in
// declaration order, so it silently resolves `main`'s call to `helper` to
// the LAST declaration (the `Buffer` one) while the emitted `CalleeID`
// still names the shared, ambiguous ID both functions carry. This program
// therefore checks CLEAN on the `check` side alone -- zero diagnostics --
// even though two functions collide on one identity.
//
// `main` calls `helper` with a Buffer argument -- matching the LAST
// declaration's parameter type, exactly the one `buildCalleeContracts`
// resolves the call to -- so `check`'s own diagnostics stay clean; the
// first declaration (`Byte` -> `Byte`) is unreferenced and checks fine on
// its own. This keeps the refusal this fixture proves attributable
// entirely to the peer: had the call instead mismatched the resolved
// contract, `check.call_argument_type_mismatch` would fire FIRST (07-10's
// stated precedence, edge 3) and mask the very defect this fixture exists
// to demonstrate.
//
// `corevalidate.Validate` independently re-derives function-ID uniqueness
// from the emitted core.Program alone (`v.unique(functionIDs, function.ID,
// "core.duplicate_function_id")`) and refuses this program with
// `core.duplicate_function_id`. Before 07-10, that refusal reached only
// `lang interface core` / `lang interface export`, and there only as
// `tool.operation_failed` / exit 3 with the code discarded -- `lang check`
// reported `status: pass`, exit 0, on this exact program. As of 07-10,
// `CheckCommandFile` consults the peer and this program is refused at the
// gate users actually run (07-REVIEW.md CR-04 / PVG-03).
//
// The CHECK-SIDE half of WR-01 -- a span-bearing `name.duplicate_function`
// diagnostic at the second declaration site, and the ambiguous-`CalleeID`
// hazard in `buildCalleeContracts` itself -- is DELIBERATELY CARRIED, not
// closed here. It needs its own ratified diagnostic code string and its own
// mutation kill; see PHASE-07-DEBT.md D-07-50.
//
// This fixture must never be added to `phase07DispatchFixtures` or to any
// list that expects a clean check, in the same way `cycle_self.lang` never
// is: it is a standing negative control for the peer-consult channel, not
// an accepting fixture.

module phase07.duplicate_function_name

export {
  fn main
}

fn helper(v: Byte) -> Byte {
  v
}

fn helper(v: Buffer) -> Buffer {
  v
}

fn main(value: Buffer) -> Buffer {
  let result = helper(value)
  result
}
